  "investigation": "DECLARED SYNTHETIC RUN: synthetic-rerun-2026-10-02 was never dispatched; its manifest declares itself synthetic and its reuse decisions are what runner.phase8_reuse.validate_reuse_candidate returned over the live world on 2026-10-02 (not_reused, fingerprint_mismatch, for all three drafting nodes). The three planner_narrower rows disagree on granularity, not on fact. The scheduler fingerprints docs/tier3_project_instantiation/ as a whole, so a changed due month in workpackage_seed.json or milestones_seed.json invalidates every drafting node. The planner traces record-level inputs: for arm 1 the excellence section reaches D3.2 only through T3.2 and partner P08 (a transitive hit), and for arm 2 the excellence section reaches MS4 through D6.1, T6.1 and P03 while the impact section reaches it only because MS4 validates its input D3.2; neither section lists the changed record as a direct input, so the planner asks reuse-under-policy. The narrower verdict is defensible because the changed field (due_month) does not alter any record those two sections draw on directly, and the conservative verdict is safe because a redraft costs quota, not correctness. No reuse policy is recorded for this world, so the operative verdict stays the scheduler's rerun; the disagreement is the directory-level fingerprint, which subticket D does not change. Recorded in docs/tier4_orchestration_state/decision_log/demo-change-scenarios-synthetic-rerun_2026-10-02.json; the acceptance boxes 3 to 5 of subticket B stay open."
